    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **68 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field), documenting the `<TIER>_<AREA>` format and the four possible values.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the derivation:\n   - A `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", expression = \"java(ownerSegment(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - A new `ownerSegment(Owner)` default method:\n     - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD` (reusing the existing effective-level accessor, which honors the stored/capped level).\n     - **AREA** = `METRO` when `locality(owner)` is in `{NSW, VIC, QLD}`, else `REGIONAL` (reusing the existing locality derivation, so it's consistent with the `locality`/`timezone` fields).\n   - A `METRO_REGIONS` constant set and the `java.util.Set` import.\n\nThe two new `Cp55Tests` (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one) pass, as does the whole suite.",
